{
 "id": "Hall",
 "notes": [
  "Set metres: she stands at the origin, the camera (level, 1.06 m up, calibration/Hall.place.json) looks into the hall along +Y.",
  "Laid out round that camera from the reference (its frames 600-713 are one still picture behind her; their median is the plate): the left wall where its foot meets the floor in the picture, the lockers where their corners' rays meet that wall; the saucer hung over the hall, its two hoops and the cove round them are circles about one upright axis 9 m from the camera (the crystal's, the picture alone does not fix the depth), each fitted to the plate's lines of light and edges (the cove's foot 2.73 m up and its top 3.96 m, 4.28 m round, running on straight towards the camera past the axis's left; the saucer's rim 3.03 m round, its hoops 3.72 m and 2.45 m, the glowing foot of its hollow 2.03 m round 3.21 m up); the crystal hangs from the hollow to just above the floor, its chains and the rod before it where the plate shows them; windows of light to the right, a terminal at the far right, two lanes painted on the floor along the wall.",
  "As the picture comes in out of the glitch (frames 543-560) crows fly through the hall round her and out (Crows).",
  "Her name, LA PLUMA, behind her is the shot's underlay (shots/Hall.json), not the set's.",
  "The windows on the right glow at 0.9: seen through the shot's exposure they come to the light grey the reference shows there (a display value of about 170), not white; the window lamp lights the hall.",
  "The deck's edge is a strip of light (Deck Light, warm): the reference's lockers and wall warm towards their feet.",
  "The right side as the plate shows it: the partition's near part (to 12 m along it) a solid wall with a yellowed trim stripe 8.5 m along, its far part glass before the bright windows; the terminal a monitor (a dark housing, a glass screen) with a pole beside it.",
  "The crystal's net is a fine gold mesh (cells about 2.5 cm, the gold over most of it) crumpled into folds a hand wide, its hem wandering; below it the dark glassy core shows, as the reference's lower third.",
  "The hall's lamps light the hall alone; she and her scythe are lit by a key of her own (Key, soft, from the windows' side before her, its power fitted from her face: fit_skin.py) and the hall's sky.",
  "The hall's sky (the world: the daylight its windows and bounce shed everywhere, on her too) is neutral, its strength fitted -- its warm light is its lamps' and glows'; a yellow zenith lit her and her scythe olive.",
  "The hall is lit as a room: a light probe volume over it (Hall Air) carries the light of its windows, glows and lamps bounced off every wall, floor and ceiling, seen or not -- without it EEVEE bounced only what the screen shows, the partition on the right stood dark grey where the reference's glows, and a lamp lying on the floor stood in for the floor's bounce."
 ],
